bug as seen in #106477\r\n\r\nBefore this PR, whenever `Control::set_position` or `Control::set_size` was called, they would \"freeze\" the container's minimum size by fixing its offsets. If the Container was made smaller by resizing/deleting a child node (e.g., an `HBoxContainer` with a child deleted) after `set_position` or `set_size` had been called, it would not shrink to match the new expected size. \r\n\r\nThis PR introduces an offset recalculation in `Control::_update_minimum_size` before `_size_changed()` is called, which fixes the issue. \r\n\r\nBefore PR\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4f9bcaae-690a-46f9-94d9-a1a41a394654\r\n\r\nAfter PR\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/00f1d6f2-4fe8-4477-8faa-2a7bc006a813\r\n\r\n*Note: I don't know why the recordings are so messed up but they show the behavior and fix, so good enough for me*","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-11-07T22:31:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T08:49:16Z","closed_at":"2025-11-15T23:09:14Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"bf7dced76918f58a55b0dcd30944b6302e6da4bd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"StarryWorm:control-shrink-fix","ref":"control-shrink-fix","repo":{"id":1060428280,"node_id":"R_kgD